  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Gu are the essence of heaven and earth, and a Gu Master is someone who has opened an aperture and uses primeval essence to feed, refine, and manipulate them.",
      "chapters": [
        7
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "what-a-gu-is",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_gu_master"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "All Gu worms have only one ability.",
      "chapters": [
        105
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "what-a-gu-is",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Without food, Gu worms die of hunger.",
      "chapters": [
        63
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "what-a-gu-is",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Rare Gu that appear on the market are snatched at once.",
      "chapters": [
        50
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "what-a-gu-is",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "A Gu Master too weak to hold one can have it taken by force.",
      "chapters": [
        43
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "what-a-gu-is",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Gu can be found in the wild, not only through academy pick or trade. When a thunder crown wolf dies, wild Gu abandon its body, and Gu Masters scramble to catch them.",
      "chapters": [
        167
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "what-a-gu-is",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_wild_gu",
        "fac_gu_masters"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Gu are also traded for primeval stones. A visiting caravan runs bidding for rare worms such as Liquor worm.",
      "chapters": [
        110
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "what-a-gu-is",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_liquor_worm"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan sells rank one healing grass Gu through a shopkeeper so clansmen can buy them. Ill-intent customers are sent to wreck Fang Yuan’s wine tavern as personal harassment from a family grudge, not as ordinary business rivalry.",
      "chapters": [
        107
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "what-a-gu-is",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "For Fang Yuan, money and fortune are just material goods; only cultivation is the root.",
      "chapters": [
        112
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "what-a-gu-is",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Gu can be taken. Fang Yuan already owns a Liquor worm when he feeds it monkey wine in a wine shop to display what he holds.",
      "chapters": [
        44
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "what-a-gu-is",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He later tracks another Liquor worm opportunity to a treehouse.",
      "chapters": [
        109
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "what-a-gu-is",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "He enters the bidding for that second worm.",
      "chapters": [
        110
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "what-a-gu-is",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "He wins, so the second Liquor worm is already in his possession.",
      "chapters": [
        111
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "what-a-gu-is",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "He fuses the two Liquor worms into a Four Flavours Liquor worm.",
      "chapters": [
        121
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "what-a-gu-is",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_four_flavors_liquor_worm"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The Gu Yue academy sends newly awakened youths to pick a vital Gu from the academy’s Gu room.",
      "chapters": [
        7
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "moonlight-gu-as-an-early-case",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_gu_yue_clan",
        "sys_vital_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Moonlight Gu is the clan’s local specialty: a rank one breed cultivated by secret method, light as paper and small enough to sit in a palm. Fang Yuan chooses one when he still has no lead on a Liquor worm.",
      "chapters": [
        8
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "moonlight-gu-as-an-early-case",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_moonlight_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "A Gu must be fed, and what it eats is specific to the Gu. This is the recurring cost of cultivation and the reason a Gu Master’s finances matter as much as their strength. Normally speaking, the higher the rank, the longer the interval between meals: a rank two Gu usually feeds every half a month, and a rank three every month or longer, while higher rank still costs more food on average.",
      "chapters": [
        100
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "feeding",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Owning a Gu and being able to keep it alive are different things. Early on, Fang Yuan declines to take a dead clansman’s Gu: clan rules treat those worms as inheritance, taking them risks exposure, and he also passes up Gu he cannot afford to feed.",
      "chapters": [
        96
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "feeding",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Gu are ranked on the same nine-level scale as Gu Masters. Gu Masters at rank one normally use rank one Gu, because higher rank Gu cost more to feed and to activate.",
      "chapters": [
        8
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "ranks-of-gu",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "The full ladder as a system statement is covered on ranks and realms.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "ranks-of-gu",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_ranks_and_realms"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The Gu Yue clan holds an Awakening Ceremony for its fifteen-year-old youths.",
      "chapters": [
        4
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "getting-a-first-gu",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_awakening_ceremony"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The ceremony grades talent and, when it succeeds, forms an aperture in the child’s body.",
      "chapters": [
        5
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "getting-a-first-gu",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "After the aperture opens and the primeval sea coagulates, those youths are rank one Gu Masters. The academy then sends them to the academy Gu room to pick a Gu worm to refine as their vital Gu.",
      "chapters": [
        7
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "getting-a-first-gu",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Everything after that is acquisition, whether by purchase, by hunting, or by taking.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "getting-a-first-gu",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "When Fang Yuan moves to refine Second Aperture Gu, rank five is mortal, rank six is immortal, and refining an Immortal Gu requires immortal essence as a basic condition.",
      "chapters": [
        377
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "immortal-gu",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_second_aperture_gu",
        "sys_immortal_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Immortal Gu continue above that divide, including rank nine Immortal Gu.",
      "chapters": [
        657
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "immortal-gu",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "How refinement works is covered on refinement.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "immortal-gu",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_refinement"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Immortal Gu are rare enough that recognising an unknown one is its own difficulty. One identification method is to consume immortal essence to activate the Immortal Gu and watch the effect, but immortal essence is precious, a wrong activation can harm the user, and some Immortal Gu show nothing unless the target or environment fits.",
      "chapters": [
        663
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "immortal-gu",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Activation cost is not the same for every Immortal Gu: attitude Gu can be activated with mental energy and used by rank six Gu Immortals even though it is rank eight.",
      "chapters": [
        1083
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "immortal-gu",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_attitude_gu",
        "sys_gu_immortal"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Primeval and immortal essence are covered on aperture and primeval essence.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "immortal-gu",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_aperture_and_primeval_essence"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "See Spring Autumn Cicada.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "immortal-gu",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_spring_autumn_cicada"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Gu are also the essence of the world and carriers of the Great Dao, and a Gu worm has one ability. A killer move is an assembly of different Gu stacking those single abilities.",
      "chapters": [
        573
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
